Third-party projects

None of these is committed here. The build image fetches each at the
revision pinned in docker/pins.env, and each stays under its own license;
see its repository.

  ssb-decomp-re        https://github.com/VetriTheRetri/ssb-decomp-re
                       The Super Smash Bros. decompilation. Declares no
                       license. About 170 of its .c files are compiled
                       unmodified, its headers are on the include path, and
                       the asset tools read its sources. Much of src/ is
                       ported from it (see LICENSE).
  KallistiOS           https://github.com/KallistiOS/KallistiOS
                       The Dreamcast OS and libraries. The host baker
                       (src/game/ssb64/hoststubs/bakepvr.c) compiles a part
                       of its pvr_prim.c, cut out at build time; the port's
                       AICA firmware (src/dc/aica/) links
                       its sound/arm/crt0.s and aica.c, compiled from the
                       image's tree.
                       The Xbox port's KallistiOS layer (Platform/xbox/)
                       reimplements KOS's API over the Xbox with KOS's own
                       names, types, constants and struct layouts, and
                       carries code ported from KOS itself:
                       dc/sound/aica_comm.h (copied), aica_cmd_iface.h and
                       aica.h, the channel routines in aica/aica_fw_xbox.c
                       (sound/arm/aica.c), kos_vmu_pkg.c
                       (util/vmu_pkg.c), the sound-RAM allocator and queue
                       in aica/aica_bus_xbox.c (sound/snd_mem.c,
                       snd_iface.c), and pvr_poly_compile and the twiddle
                       in pvr_xbox.c (hardware/pvr/). These stay under the
                       KOS License (BSD), whose text is
                       Platform/xbox/LICENSE.KOS.
  glankk/n64           https://github.com/glankk/n64
                       gfxdis, the reference display-list disassembler used
                       by tools/check/verify_dl.py.
  sh4zam               https://github.com/gyrovorbis/sh4zam
                       SH-4 math routines.
  img4dc               https://github.com/Kazade/img4dc
                       The .cdi disc-image builder.
  dreamcast-toolchain  docker.io/pcercuei/dreamcast-toolchain
                       The prebuilt SH-4 cross-compiler image.

